1
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,960
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

2
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:10,050
None of that. Not while you're living under my roof.

3
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:12,050
What?

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,300
Look, just because I know about you two doesn't mean I like looking at it.

5
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:19,220
Aren't you supposed to be at an audition for another hour?

6
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:22,350
Well, I'm sorry if I'm not a middle-aged black woman.

7
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:28,230
And I'm also sorry if sometimes I go to the wrong audition.

8
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:32,610
Okay, look, if I have to pretend I don't know about you two...

9
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:36,110
...then you two are gonna have to pretend there's nothing to know about.

10
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:38,870
Okay, sorry.

11
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:46,540
I can hear that.

12
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:49,880
Rachel's at work.

13
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,590
I can still hear you.

14
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:47,560
Hey.

15
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:47,560
Hey.

16
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:48,940
Hey. What's that?

17
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:53,020
Yeah, my mom sent me a family heirloom that once belonged to my grandmother.

18
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:54,270
Can you believe it?

19
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,070
A year ago I didn't even have a family...

20
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,490
...and now I have heirlooms for crying out loud.

21
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:10,960
Oh, God!

22
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:10,960
Aah!

23
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:14,130
Oh, soft.

24
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:16,710
Is this mink?

25
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:16,710
Yeah.

26
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:22,050
Why would my mother send me a fur? Doesn't she know me but at all?

27
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:27,060
Plus, I have a perfectly fine coat that no innocent animals suffered to make.

28
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:30,270
Yeah, just some 9-year-old Filipino kids who worked their fingers bloody...

29
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:32,020
...for 12 cents an hour.

30
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:36,530
That didn't happen, I made that up.

31
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,360
Hey.

32
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,360
Ross?

33
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:44,160
Ross, you can't put up flyers in here.

34
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:46,370
How come? Everybody else does.

35
00:02:47,330 --> 00:02:48,790
You can't.

36
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:52,920
What is that?

37
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:57,000
Oh, uh, I'm getting rid of a couple of things.

38
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,210
This is all of your things.

39
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,300
Yes, yes, it is.

40
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:06,350
No, but it's good. Emily thinks we should get all new stuff.

41
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:09,560
Stuff that's just ours. Together, you know, brand new.

42
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:12,730
So basically this is a "getting rid of anything Rachel ever touched" sale.

43
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,730
Touched, used, sat on, slept on...

44
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:17,730
I'll take it all.

45
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:20,940
Hey, Ross, you're okay with that?

46
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,030
Look, if I can just do what Emily wants...

47
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,030
...and get her to New York, I'm sure everything will be fine.

48
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,290
Okay, but don't you think that's a little extreme?

49
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:32,660
After what I did, can you blame her?

50
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:32,660
Oh, my God. You got off easy.

51
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:35,500
When my friend Sylvie's husband said someone else's name in bed...

52
00:03:35,670 --> 00:03:38,250
...she cursed him and turned his thingy green.

53
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,100
What is he doing?

54
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:51,520
Emily thinks Ross' furniture has got Rachel cooties?

55
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:53,640
Calm down, Joey.

56
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:53,640
No.

57
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,980
Everything's getting all messed up, you know?

58
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,980
Emily won't let Ross see Rachel.

59
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:02,950
We're not gonna stop seeing Rachel, hence, Ross stops seeing us.

60
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,530
Oh, I hate this. Everything's changing.

61
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:08,410
Yeah, I know. We're losing Ross, Joey said "hence."

62
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:17,080
I'm not happy about this either, but, you know, if Ross says he's happy...

63
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:20,300
...then we just have to keep our feelings about Emily to ourselves.

64
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,840
Are you cool with that?

65
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:23,510
No.

66
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:27,430
But, you know, I'm an actor.

67
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,470
I'll act cool.

68
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:39,940
Ooh. Oh, God, storage rooms give me the creeps.

69
00:04:40,150 --> 00:04:42,360
Monica, please, hurry up, honey, please.

70
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:44,070
If you want the little round waffles...

71
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:47,200
...you've gotta wait till I find the little round waffle iron.

72
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:50,200
I want the little round waffles.

73
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:50,200
All right.

74
00:04:50,370 --> 00:04:51,410
Here it is.

75
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:55,210
Right underneath the can of bug bomb.

76
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:59,920
I wonder if the best place to put something that cooks food is underneath the poison?

77
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,960
Okay, you know what? I'll have toast.

78
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:10,010
Fog him! Fog him!

79
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:18,690
I don't know what I'm gonna do about this coat.

80
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,360
I'll take it.

81
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:23,980
That might work.

82
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:23,980
Oh, yeah, ha, ha.

83
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,410
Huh? All right, what do you think?

84
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:32,870
You're on in five, Ms. Minnelli.

85
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:38,120
No, no, no, it's just a bit sudden.

86
00:05:38,370 --> 00:05:41,210
No, it's great, okay? I am totally on board.

87
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,630
I love you too. All right, bye.

88
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:51,010
What's the matter, Ross?

89
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:51,010
Nothing. No. Oh, uh, actually...

90
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,850
...great news. Heh.

91
00:05:53,010 --> 00:05:54,600
Um, just got off the phone with Emily...

92
00:05:54,770 --> 00:05:57,980
...and looks like I'm moving to a new apartment.

93
00:05:58,140 --> 00:05:59,390
Whoo-hoo!

94
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:04,900
Why?

95
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:04,900
Well, her thought is... And I agree.

96
00:06:05,150 --> 00:06:09,400
Fresh new furniture, why not a fresh new apartment?

97
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:11,370
Her cousin has this great place to sublet.

98
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:14,490
It's got a view of the river on one side and Columbia on the other.

99
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:17,000
That's way uptown. That's like three trains away...

100
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,910
...which is great.

101
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,210
I love to ride that rail.

102
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,590
So you're really okay with this?

103
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,510
Yes, yes. I mean, it's kind of far from work...

104
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,970
...but, uh, you know, I'll get so much done on the commute.

105
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:34,850
I've been given the gift of time.

106
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:38,980
That's so funny, because last Christmas I got the gift of space.

107
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:43,060
We should get them together and make a continuum.

108
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,570
Now he's moving?

109
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:52,410
Man, what is Emily doing to him? Ow!

110
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,910
He's not even here.

111
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,950
You guys. You guys.

112
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:01,920
We were just in the storage area and we saw this really creepy man.

113
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:04,840
He was like this crazy-eyed, hairy beast-man.

114
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,590
He was like a Bigfoot or a yeti or something.

115
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:12,760
He came at us with an ax, so Rachel had to use the bug bomb on him.

116
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:16,350
Yeah, I pulled the tab and I just fogged his yeti ass.

117
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:20,810
Uh, like, dark hair, bushy beard?

118
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:23,480
Yeah.

119
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:23,480
Yeah, you fogged Danny.

120
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:28,020
Ugh, please. We did not fog Danny.

121
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:29,610
Who's Danny?

122
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,740
Danny just moved in downstairs.

123
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:36,580
He just got back from this four-month trek in the Andes. Nice fella.

124
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:40,080
Oh, he's nice. He's nice. You know, you always...

125
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:43,000
...stick up for the people we fog.

126
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:54,220
Yeah?

127
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:54,220
Hi.

128
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:58,640
You might not remember us, but we are the girls that fogged you.

129
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:01,560
We're really sorry we fogged you.

130
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:01,560
Yeah.

131
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:03,770
Okay.

132
00:08:09,650 --> 00:08:13,070
Hi, uh, just so you know, we didn't mean to fog you.

133
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:16,490
We actually thought you were like a yeti or something.

134
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:18,660
Okay.

135
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,160
Yes?

136
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:26,420
Hi. Ahem, sorry to bother you...

137
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:29,920
...but I don't think that we can accept your acceptance of our apology.

138
00:08:30,130 --> 00:08:32,920
It just doesn't really seem like you mean it.

139
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:35,590
Okay.

140
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:41,010
Wow. That guy is so rude.

141
00:08:41,270 --> 00:08:43,680
Really. What is with that guy?

142
00:08:43,850 --> 00:08:46,140
I mean, you'd forgive me if I fogged you.

143
00:08:46,850 --> 00:08:48,230
Well, you did, a little bit.

144
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,900
Oh, my God, honey. I'm so sorry.

145
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,440
I totally forgive you.

146
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,440
Really?

147
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,200
Hey.

148
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,200
Hey.

149
00:09:01,370 --> 00:09:04,620
So listen, you know my friend Chris who owns the crematorium?

150
00:09:04,870 --> 00:09:07,250
Crematorium Chris? Sure.

151
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:11,670
Well, he said that he would cremate my fur coat for free...

152
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:15,380
...if I, um, you know, bring in the next person I know who dies.

153
00:09:19,010 --> 00:09:20,600
Oh, my God.

154
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:23,100
Oh, my God. Look at these pelts.

155
00:09:24,350 --> 00:09:26,520
Don't get too attached. She's having it cremated.

156
00:09:26,690 --> 00:09:28,060
What...?

157
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,650
Phoebe? Ha. Honey?

158
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:34,730
Honey, I know you're quirky, and I get a big kick out of it. We all do, actually.

159
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:36,990
But if you destroy a coat like this...

160
00:09:37,150 --> 00:09:40,660
...I mean, that is like a crime against nature.

161
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,290
Not nature. Fashion.

162
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,200
This is fashion?

163
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:47,790
Okay, so to you, death is fashion?

164
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,790
That's really funny. Yeah, here's Phoebe, uh...

165
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:55,260
...sporting, you know, cutting-edge hairy carcass...

166
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:59,470
...from, you know, the steel traps of wintry Russia.

167
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:03,100
I mean, you really think this looks good?

168
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,430
Because I do.

169
00:10:12,190 --> 00:10:14,440
I know, I miss you too. I can't wait to see you.

170
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:16,150
I love you. Bye.

171
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:18,360
Okay, what is in here, rocks?

172
00:10:18,990 --> 00:10:21,910
No, this is my collection of, uh, fossil samples.

173
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,950
So rocks.

174
00:10:33,590 --> 00:10:35,340
I'm really gonna miss this apartment. Heh.

175
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:39,630
You know, Ben took his first steps right over there.

176
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:44,390
Hey, remember when I ran into this thing and it kind of knocked me out a little?

177
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:47,930
I love this place.

178
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,890
To tell you the truth, I wish I didn't have to move.

179
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:56,320
Uh, are you saying that you're not entirely happy about this?

180
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:59,030
Well, I mean, if, uh, Emily gave me a choice...

181
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,320
You do have a choice.

182
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:04,990
Ross, why are you listening to her? Are you crazy?

183
00:11:05,450 --> 00:11:06,490
What?

184
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:10,410
It's not right what Emily wants you to do. She is totally... Ow!

185
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,710
Stop pinching me.

186
00:11:13,290 --> 00:11:17,630
You guys said I only had to keep my mouth shut as long as Ross was happy, right?

187
00:11:18,510 --> 00:11:21,970
Well, he just told me that he's not entirely happy.

188
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,680
What's going on?

189
00:11:25,850 --> 00:11:27,010
We all hate Emily.

190
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,810
No.

191
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,810
No, Ross, we do not hate Emily.

192
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:35,980
We just think that you're having to sacrifice...

193
00:11:36,190 --> 00:11:38,110
...a whole lot to make her happy.

194
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,650
Yeah.

195
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:44,410
We just think that maybe she's being a little unreasonable.

196
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,570
Yes, yes, unreasonable.

197
00:11:47,030 --> 00:11:48,870
Unreasonable?

198
00:11:49,450 --> 00:11:52,710
How about we have this conversation when one of you guys gets married?

199
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:56,840
You have no idea what it takes to make a marriage work.

200
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:59,630
It's about compromise. Do you always like it? No.

201
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:00,960
Do you do it? Yes.

202
00:12:01,170 --> 00:12:04,510
Because it's not all laughing, happy, candy in the sky...

203
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,970
...drinking coffee at Central Perk all the time. It's real life, okay?

204
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:11,390
It's what grownups do.

205
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,570
I think he's right.

206
00:12:19,730 --> 00:12:22,070
You guys hang out at the coffeehouse way too much.

207
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:32,410
God, I feel so guilty about Ross.

208
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:32,410
Ugh, I know.

209
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,330
I kind of feel like it's my fault.

210
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:39,290
Kind of?

211
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:42,550
If you just kept this to yourself, none of this would have happened.

212
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,220
Well, I'm keeping so many things to myself these days...

213
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:47,050
...something was bound to slip out.

214
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:51,810
Well, I think it's very brave what you said.

215
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:57,690
I can't sit here anymore. I have to walk places.

216
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:01,570
Pheebs, what are you doing with the coat? How about the whole animal rights thing?

217
00:13:01,730 --> 00:13:04,940
Well, ahem, I've been reading up, and for your information...

218
00:13:05,150 --> 00:13:06,990
...minks are not very nice.

219
00:13:08,990 --> 00:13:11,660
Okay, I admit it. I love this coat, okay?

220
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:16,290
It's the best thing I've ever had wrapped around me, including Phil Huntley.

221
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:20,170
Remember Phil Huntley? He was fine.

222
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:32,720
Hi.

223
00:13:35,850 --> 00:13:37,940
So you like the short hair better?

224
00:13:35,850 --> 00:13:37,940
What?

225
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:42,900
Yeti? Uh, Danny?

226
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:47,490
I had to cut my hair to get rid of the, uh...

227
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:49,740
...fogger smell.

228
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:54,040
Listen, I'm so sorry. I would have never fogged you...

229
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:57,540
...you know, if you hadn't looked so... You know, um...

230
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:01,540
Absolutely. Some people are just into appearances.

231
00:14:02,130 --> 00:14:04,250
What?

232
00:14:02,130 --> 00:14:04,250
That's cool. That's cool.

233
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:07,090
What...? Hey, whoa, no, no, no, that is not cool.

234
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,720
You don't even know me.

235
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:11,930
Come on. You got the shopping bags and the Saks catalogue.

236
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:16,220
So from that, you think you've got me all figured out?

237
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:17,770
Well, you don't.

238
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:22,310
You know, I could have toys for underprivileged kids in here.

239
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:24,480
Do you?

240
00:14:24,650 --> 00:14:28,360
Well, you know, if kids like to play with capri pants.

241
00:14:29,530 --> 00:14:30,570
Okay.

242
00:14:31,990 --> 00:14:34,080
And stop saying that. I hate that.

243
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:35,740
Okay.

244
00:14:46,590 --> 00:14:49,340
Fine. I judged you. I made a snap judgment.

245
00:14:49,550 --> 00:14:51,090
But you did it too, and you're worse...

246
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:53,970
...because you are sticking to your stupid snap judgment.

247
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:57,430
You can't even open up your mind for a second to see that you might be wrong.

248
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,140
What does that say about you?

249
00:15:00,230 --> 00:15:02,690
That pizza place across the street any good?

250
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,730
What?

251
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,730
I'm hungry.

252
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:07,610
You wanna get some pizza? You can keep yelling if there's more.

253
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:09,780
Okay.

254
00:15:10,570 --> 00:15:14,240
Okay.

255
00:15:10,570 --> 00:15:14,240
Stop saying that. I hate that.

256
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,950
Uh, Ross?

257
00:15:20,830 --> 00:15:22,330
Are you still mad at us?

258
00:15:20,830 --> 00:15:22,330
Yup.

259
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:25,040
Oh, good, because we have an "I'm Sorry" song. Ha, ha.

260
00:15:25,210 --> 00:15:27,300
You know what? I'm really not in the mood.

261
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:29,880
Look, Ross.

262
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:34,890
I feel really bad. I mean, you're going through all this stuff...

263
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,220
...and I just acted like a jerk.

264
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:41,350
Yeah, we are so sorry.

265
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:41,350
You're stepping on the song.

266
00:15:41,890 --> 00:15:46,150
Look, we were way out of line, all right? We totally support you.

267
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,440
Whatever you decide, whatever you do.

268
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:51,740
Okay, now you're just taking lines right out of the song.

269
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:56,820
Look, this is hard enough, okay? I really need you guys right now.

270
00:15:57,080 --> 00:16:00,120
Yes, exactly. And that's why...

271
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:05,080
Why don't you come over tonight, and I'll make you your favorite dinner?

272
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:07,210
Come on.

273
00:16:07,710 --> 00:16:09,630
Okay.

274
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,630
Thanks, you guys.

275
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:13,340
Pheebs, are you wearing fur?

276
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:15,590
Okay, let's get some perspective, people.

277
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:19,100
It's not like I'm wearing a seeing-eye dog coat.

278
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:27,650
You know, Ross, I, uh, think I kind of understand why I lost it today.

279
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:30,610
You do, huh?

280
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:30,610
Yeah, you see, um...

281
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,990
...I'm an actor, right?

282
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:36,820
So I gotta keep my emotions right at the surface, you know?

283
00:16:37,450 --> 00:16:40,450
I got a lot of balls in the air, you know what I mean?

284
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:47,250
It's tough. Guys like me, you know, you wander around, you're alone.

285
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:50,750
What are you talking about?

286
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:53,720
I'm not sure.

287
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:57,800
Hi.

288
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:57,800
Hey, look at you. Where have you been?

289
00:16:58,010 --> 00:17:00,720
Oh, I went to have pizza. With Danny.

290
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:05,810
How did that happen?

291
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:05,810
That yeti is one smooth talker.

292
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:09,310
I hope you're not too full, because dinner's almost ready.

293
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:12,730
Yeah, you know, I think I'm probably just gonna hang out in my room.

294
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,110
Oh, no.

295
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,110
Why?

296
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:15,570
Come on, you guys.

297
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:18,870
Listen, if Emily knew I was here having dinner with you, she would flip out...

298
00:17:19,030 --> 00:17:20,660
...and you know it.

299
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:24,910
It's okay. I really... I don't mind.

300
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:27,920
Wait, wait, wait. You know what? Just stay.

301
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,830
Please.

302
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:32,670
It would really mean a lot for me if you stay.

303
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:35,340
Ross, I just...

304
00:17:35,510 --> 00:17:38,970
Rachel, please, just have dinner with us.

305
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,140
Okay, Joey, it's okay. Settle down.

306
00:17:42,350 --> 00:17:44,810
All right. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

307
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:47,100
You see, Rach, I'm an actor.

308
00:17:50,900 --> 00:17:54,650
Hey. Hey, look. Ugly naked guy's back.

309
00:17:57,070 --> 00:17:58,820
We haven't seen him in so long.

310
00:17:59,070 --> 00:18:02,530
Oh, God. I really missed that fat bastard.

311
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:07,960
Wow. This is so weird.

312
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:11,920
I just realized this may be the last time we're all hanging out together.

313
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,840
It's almost as if he knew.

314
00:18:17,630 --> 00:18:19,010
I'll get it.

315
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,140
Hello?

316
00:18:24,010 --> 00:18:25,470
Hi, Emily.

317
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:29,560
Yeah, uh, you tracked him down. Hold on one second.

318
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,900
Hey.

319
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:37,530
Yeah, yeah, we're, uh, just having dinner.

320
00:18:38,110 --> 00:18:39,650
Uh, yeah, sure, hold on.

321
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,450
She wants to say hi. Hold on.

322
00:18:44,740 --> 00:18:45,950
Hi, Emily.

323
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,620
Hello, everyone.

324
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:49,910
So who am I saying hello to?

325
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:52,960
Well, uh, I don't know about who's here...

326
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:56,880
...but I can tell you for damn sure who's not here, and that's Rachel.

327
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:03,010
Well, I should hope not. Ross knows better than that by now.

328
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:09,060
You know what? Uh, Rachel is here.

329
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,020
She's there?

330
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:13,230
Oh, yeah, there she is.

331
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,940
Yeah. Yeah, she's here.

332
00:19:17,110 --> 00:19:18,900
Ross, take me off speakerphone.

333
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:23,530
Hi.

334
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:23,530
How could you do this to me?

335
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:26,580
I thought I'd made my feelings about Rachel perfectly clear.

336
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:30,790
Look, Emily, I'm just having dinner with my friends, okay?

337
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:34,380
You obviously can't keep away from her.

338
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:34,380
That's ridiculous.

339
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:38,880
Look, I'm moving for you. I'm cutting friends out of my life for you.

340
00:19:39,050 --> 00:19:42,470
Please, just get on the plane and come to New York, okay?

341
00:19:42,630 --> 00:19:45,970
You'll see you're the only person I want to be with.

342
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:50,430
I'll feel better when I'm there and I can know where you are all the time.

343
00:19:51,770 --> 00:19:57,190
Well, you can't know where I am all the time.

344
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:01,940
Look, this marriage is never gonna work if you don't trust me.

345
00:20:03,990 --> 00:20:05,160
You're right.

346
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:10,160
So... can you trust me?

347
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,210
No.

348
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,590
I think it's going okay.

349
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:23,590
Looks like he's smiling.

350
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,680
How can you tell? You can only see the back of his head.

351
00:20:27,550 --> 00:20:29,310
You can totally tell.

352
00:20:29,470 --> 00:20:30,970
Here, look, watch me.

353
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:37,770
Smile. Frown. Smile. Frown. Smile.

354
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,120
Well, I guess that's it.

355
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:55,960
Why? What happened?

356
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:57,790
My marriage is over.

357
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:00,540
What?

358
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:00,540
Oh, sweetie.

359
00:21:01,090 --> 00:21:03,550
Oh, look at you, you're shivering.

360
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:05,840
Here.

361
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:12,310
Ross, honey, is there anything we can do?

362
00:21:14,390 --> 00:21:15,560
Yeah.

363
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:20,020
You can help me get my furniture back from Gunther.

364
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,880
Okay, stop tormenting me.

365
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:48,630
This is mink, okay? They're mean, and they hate squirrels.

366
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:51,890
And, you know, most of these probably wanted to be coats.

367
00:21:53,930 --> 00:21:57,560
All right, fine. No, I get it. Here.

368
00:21:57,810 --> 00:21:58,850
You take it.

369
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:02,230
Are you happy now? I'm cold.

